          "path": "_m/c/2/j/m/battle-of-cottonwood-wk/nez-perce-war-foster-s-gravesi.jpg",
          "filename": "Nez Perce War - Foster's Gravesite, Idaho Historical Marker No. 500, Cottonwood, Idaho (31499232447).jpg",
          "caption": "“I will not hide anything. That part of the fight was not long.” Yellow Wolf, Nez Perce Warrior. On July 3, 1877, 2nd Lt. Sevier M. Rains, civilian scout William Foster, and ten 1st cavalrymen rode from Norton’s ranch (Cottonwood) in search of Nez Perce. Six miles northwest of here warriors attacked and killed the detachment. Foster’s grave is three miles west on Cottonwood Butte road. The soldiers’ remains were reinterred at Fort Walla Walla.",
